      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The island earned the nickname \"Emerald Isle\" for its lush green foliage that covers much of Beaver Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://glialliance.org/resources-beaver/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Beaver Island Head Lighthouse, erected in 1851, was deactivated in 1962 and is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_Island_(Lake_Michigan)",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
